      "text": "January 7, 2026 | Natural Disasters Summary \n\nOujda, Morocco | Rare snowfall blanketed the city for the first time in about 25 years. Up to 2 cm fell in the city center and 7–10 cm in nearby villages, caused by a cold air intrusion and low-pressure system.\n\nWest Halmahera, Indonesia | Severe flooding and landslides after prolonged heavy rain killed two people, damaged or destroyed hundreds of homes, and forced the evacuation of about 1,500 residents across multiple districts.\n\nDavao Oriental, Philippines | A strong offshore earthquake struck Mindanao, triggering evacuations in several communities. No casualties or major damage were reported, but authorities warned of aftershocks.\n\nAlbay Province, Philippines | Volcanic activity at Mayon intensified, prompting authorities to raise the alert level to 3. Lava dome collapse, ash plumes, and pyroclastic flows led to mass evacuations around the volcano.\n\n#Flooding #Earthquake #Volcano #Snowfall #Evacuations #ExtremeWeather #NaturalDisasters\n#ALLATRA",
